WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:06.039 align:start position:0% line:0%
Today we are on
the Illinois River in Lacon.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.540 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
- That's in America, Dan.
- Oh, thanks.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.075 align:start position:0% line:0%
What is the story
with this river?

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:10.476 size:84% position:58%
Well, in the '60s and '70s,

00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:12.145 align:start size:72% position:28%
fish farmers thought
it would be a good idea

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.781 size:88% position:56%
to import Asian carp to eat
all those unwanted plankton.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.216 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, plants, animals--
they're hungry boys.

00:00:17.249 --> 00:00:19.786 align:start size:81% position:19%
Obviously, immediately
escaped out into the river
and trashed everything.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.521 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Absolute nightmare.
- Yeah.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.689 align:start position:0%
And if you take a boat
with a shiny bottom
on this river,

00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:25.358 align:start position:0%
apparently
it startles the fish

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:27.760 align:start position:0%
and they just leap
uncontrollably out of the water.

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:29.762 align:start position:0%
So we're gonna take
our Phantom on a boat

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:33.132 align:start position:0%
and hopefully get some lovely
slow-motion shots
of flying fish.

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:35.201 align:start size:78% position:22%
You know they grow up to,
like, a hundred pounds?

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.603 align:start size:72% position:28%
That's like you
flying out of the river
and damaging boats.

00:00:37.636 --> 00:00:39.338 align:start position:0%
( laughing )
I'm not a hundred pounds.

00:00:39.371 --> 00:00:41.207 align:start position:0%
All right, well, let's go
suit up and meet the captain.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.775 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Shall we? All right.
- Yep.

00:00:42.808 --> 00:00:43.810 align:start size:9% position:91%
Oh!

00:00:50.282 --> 00:00:53.286
<i> ( music playing )</i>

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.390 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Dan: How's it going?
  Captain Nate.
- Nate: Good, good.

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.192
- How you guys doing?
- Dan: Yeah, good.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.726 size:84% position:42%
First things first, though.

00:01:00.759 --> 00:01:03.196
Anyone die doing this before?
Anyone been killed by a fish?

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.298 align:start position:0% line:0%
Nate: Nobody's ever been killed.
Just a few broken jaws,

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.266 align:start size:63% position:38% line:0%
broken noses,
nothing too serious.

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:10.503 align:start size:84% position:16%
- What?
- All right, let's go.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.841 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Nice little day out
  on the boat.
- Yeah, we'll see

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:18.745 size:81% position:59%
if that's still the case
when a fish knocks me out.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.317 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So they are just
  in different spots?
- Yeah.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.452
And when you find a school,
it's, like, crazy.

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:27.720 size:81% position:41%
Yeah, once I get a school,

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.255 align:start position:0%
I like to circle
around that school

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:31.290 align:start position:0%
and try to get 'em going
as much as possible.

00:01:31.323 --> 00:01:32.525 align:start size:44% position:56%
Rolling.

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:36.662 align:start size:34% position:66%
Whoa!

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:37.864 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Oh, I missed him.
- I didn't see that one.

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:40.299
Gav:
Yeah, yeah, whoa!

00:01:40.332 --> 00:01:41.801
There was three or four there.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.402 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Flippin'-A!
- Oh! Oh!

00:01:43.435 --> 00:01:45.338 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Fish! Gross!
- Fish in the boat!

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.507
- Crap.
- Get it.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.175 align:start size:88% position:13%
- ( laughs )
- You're all right, pal.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.376
What do you do?

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:52.612 align:start size:34% position:66%
( laughs )
What?

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.847 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Just chuck him out?
- Chuck him out.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.450 align:start size:91% position:9%
- There he goes.
- So they poop in midair.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.453 align:start position:0%
They don't have stomachs,
so they just filter food
all day long.

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:03.156 align:start position:0%
So when they jump out
of the water,
they defecate all over you.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.291
So they break your jaw
and then poo on you
for good measure.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:06.726 align:start position:0%
So when they land in your boat,
they just start bleeding,

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.529 align:start position:0%
pooping, sliming.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.564 align:start position:0%
Ah, the poop,
bleed, slime fish.
They do everything.

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:12.665
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:14.266 --> 00:02:15.735 align:start position:0%
To the left.
That's it. That's it.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.603
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:18.804
- Bloody hell.
- ( chuckles )

00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:21.174 align:start size:16% position:84%
Whoa!

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.775 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Oh, no! It's gone.
- Hold on.

00:02:22.808 --> 00:02:25.344 align:start size:59% position:41%
Oh, there's
craploads in there.

00:02:25.377 --> 00:02:26.946 align:start size:75% position:25%
Whoa!

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:28.814 align:start size:78% position:22%
- God.
- All right, stop.

00:02:28.847 --> 00:02:31.450 align:start size:56% position:44%
Stop, stop. Jesus.

00:02:31.483 --> 00:02:34.254 align:start size:69% position:31%
All right,
let's watch that back.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.359
Dan:<i> Whoa!</i>

00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:42.261
<i> That was crazy.</i>

00:02:42.294 --> 00:02:43.897 align:start position:0%
- Gav:<i> Looks nice. </i>
- Dan:<i> Yeah, it looks very nice.</i>

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:49.902 align:start size:91% position:9%
 Gav:<i> Very cinematic.
 There's just a fish
 in the background there.</i>

